XB-Kidux-Name-en: TurboWarp
XB-Kidux-Description-en: A high-performance alternative to Scratch, with the same blocks and the same projects, compiled for smoother animations and games on a slower computer.
XB-Kidux-Name-es: TurboWarp
XB-Kidux-Description-es: Versión de alto rendimiento de Scratch, con los mismos bloques y los mismos proyectos, compilada para animaciones y juegos más fluidos en un ordenador modesto.
XB-Kidux-Ages: 8-16
XB-Kidux-Before: scratchjr
Description: Kidux learning module: TurboWarp, Scratch made faster
 Kidux is a Debian derivative for a child's first computer. This learning
 module is TurboWarp: Scratch's editor with a compiler that runs projects
 many times faster, the same blocks and the same project files, for a
 slower computer or when Scratch does not run well. It is served on this
 computer and shown in Chromium, in the child's language. Its library of
 characters, backdrops and sounds comes from the internet.
 .
 Once it is installed, an adult switches it on for each child on the
 Modules page of the adult panel.
